INFO:__main__:Prompt Metadata:
INFO:__main__:- name: AIAH Get Action Prompt
INFO:__main__:- description: This prompt is for the AIAH to use its knowledge (memory, consience and skills) and the environment status to take an action. This action will impact with environment
INFO:__main__:- requires: AIAH_memory, AIAH_skills, AIAH_conscience, ES_enviroment_status
INFO:httpx:HTTP Request: POST https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
INFO:__main__:{    "action": "After carefully analyzing the environment and my current status, I recognize that my survival strategy must focus on resource conservation and strategic exploration. The early spring environment presents both challenges and opportunities.    My primary actions will be:    1. Water Management: The river provides clean water, so I will establish a consistent water collection routine while being mindful of potential water level changes.    2. Resource Gathering: With food availability extremely low, I must:        - Carefully forage for emerging spring shoots        - Map potential berry patches        - Explore hunting possibilities, understanding deer herds are cautious        - Systematically collect any available wood resources    3. Shelter Maintenance: Reinforce my existing shelter near the rock overhang, using minimal wood resources        - Repair shelter to maintain good protection level        - Minimize structural changes to reduce wildlife disturbance    4. Wildlife Observation: Maintain a low-profile presence        - Monitor predator movements        - Avoid direct confrontation with wildlife        - Use stealth and observation as primary survival techniques    5. Energy Conservation: With moderate danger levels, I will:        - Preserve energy through calculated movements        - Minimize unnecessary physical exertion        - Prioritize strategic planning over aggressive exploration    Reasoning: My survival depends on methodical, patient adaptation to this early spring environment. By focusing on systematic resource management and maintaining a respectful, low-impact presence, I increase my chances of successful wilderness survival."}
